DESCRIPTION:Get up-to-date information at: https://luma.com/event/evt-X06O9
 YIA44xbuyY?pk=g-kPozkZ7dqFxVkR2\n\nAddress:\nWatt Hall\nWatt Hall B1\nLos A
 ngeles\, California\nUnited States\n\nSEP is thrilled to host an evening wi
 th Jordan Noone—Co-founder of Relativity Space\, Embedded Ventures\, and Zo
 o AI.\nJordan built Relativity Space on a wild bet: 3D-print an entire rock
 et from scratch. That bet turned into a $4.2 billion company. From there\, 
 he built Embedded Ventures around a simple thesis: the best deep tech start
 ups should serve both commercial markets and national security. The firm no
 w manages a $100M fund and holds a first-of-its-kind partnership with the U
 .S. Space Force. His latest venture\, Zoo\, is taking on one of the most un
 touched problems in hardware: the design…\n\nHosted by Grishma Shukla & 3 o
 thers
