 alendar.google.com
UID:18896630-7537-4153-8afd-6b3efa2323d9|trojanlearn
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=El
 lie Lin-Stevens;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:elinstev@usc.edu
CREATED:20260124T172349Z
DESCRIPTION:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n  \nDear Ellie\,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nT
 his is to confirm that you have registered for the following Consent and He
 althy Relationship (CHR) virtual instructor-led training session:\n\n\n\n\n
 \n\n\n\nTraining Title:\nCHR Part 1: Trojans Respect Consent \n\n\nTraining
  Type:\n\nSession\n\n\n\nSession Number:\n\n5PM TRC 216\n\n\n\nDate(s):\n\n
 2/3/2026 to 2/3/2026\n\n\n\nTime(s):\n\n5:00 PM to 7:00 PM\n\n\n\nSession D
 uration:\n\n2 Hours 0 Minutes\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\nThis module is required f
 or undergraduates in their first/second semester and centers on understandi
 ng bodily autonomy\, identifying how power impacts consent\, and emphasizes
  respectful communication between sexual partners. Incompletion of your ass
 igned module by February 27th\, 2026 will result in a registration hold beg
 inning Summer 2026 registration. Registration holds are released immediatel
 y following session completion\, however\, completion status in MyUSC could
  be delayed up to 24 hours.  In other words\, you will not be able to regis
 ter for classes right after completing your training.\n\n\n\nYou must click
  the link below 5 minutes before the session start time to launch and atten
 d the module:\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\nLAUNCH YOUR VIRTUAL SESSION(https://shibbolet
 h.usc.edu/idp/profile/SAML2/Unsolicited/SSO?providerId=https://trojanlearn.
 csod.com/shibboleth&shire=https://trojanlearn.csod.com/samldefault.aspx&tar
 get=%252fDeepLink%252fProcessRedirect.aspx%253fmodule%253dlaunchvilttrainin
 g%2526src%253demail%2526objectId%253dc0039c0b-c0c2-4a7b-9176-61d01b870ddd%2
 526userId%253d%2525255e%2525255e%2525255enFRZMe1zComAOWt3RMF%2525252fVg%252
 5253d%2525253d)\n\n\n\n\n\nPlease note that you will need to be actively pa
 rticipating to complete your requirement. To ensure that we can have the mo
 st optimal session\, we ask the following:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPlease be sure to
  update your zoom account to the most up-to-date version.\nPlease launch th
 e session with a laptop or a computer. If you do not have access to a lapto
 p or a desktop\, please email us at sconsent@usc.edu(mailto:sconsent@usc.ed
 u) to let us know and we can assist with access to a computer in our office
 .\nPlease note that you will be asked to turn your camera on and to partici
 pate throughout the session if you are at capacity. Please make sure that y
 ou are in a quiet\, private location where you are able to participate. \nD
 o not show up to the session late or leave early. Your attention is require
 d for the full 2 hours.  Signing up for a session does not equal completion
 . Students must actively participate in the live remote session to complete
  the requirement.\n\n\nIndividuals with disabilities who need accommodation
 s to attend this event may complete the Accommodation Request Form(https://
 usc.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_3f1IF7k6z7NgudU). It is requested that indivi
 duals requiring accommodations or auxiliary aids such as sign language inte
 rpreters and alternative format materials notify us at least ten days prior
  to the event. Every reasonable effort will be made to provide reasonable a
 ccommodations in an effective and timely manner.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThank you\,\n
 \n\n \n\n\nUSC Student Health\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nQuestions about this tr
 aining?\n\n    \nPlease contact: USC Student Requirements at required@usc.e
 du(mailto:required@usc.edu).\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nThis email was generated by 
 Trojan Learn\, USC's centralized portal for learning.  Direct technical que
 stions about TrojanLearn to USC Student Requirements at required@usc.edu(ma
 ilto:required@usc.edu). Please do not reply to this email. \n\n  \n\n\n\n C
 SOD SYSTEM ID:  5597408\n
